  <h1>Gemini Takeout → readable archive</h1>
    <p class="lead">Google’s Takeout path is the dependable way to pull Gemini-related data. The dump is complete — but not friendly. TotalRecalls helps turn it into a readable local archive.</p>
    <h2>Why Takeout (not a fragile scrape)</h2>
    <p>Gemini’s web surface changes often. For v1, TotalRecalls prioritizes a <strong>filesystem Takeout folder or JSON</strong> you already downloaded from Google. That stays honest and stable.</p>
    <h2>Steps</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Create a Google Takeout that includes your Gemini / Gemini Apps data (as offered in your account region).</li>
      <li>Download and unzip the Takeout package on your PC.</li>
      <li>In TotalRecalls, choose <strong>Gemini</strong>.</li>
      <li>Paste the folder path or use <strong>Browse…</strong> to select it.</li>
      <li>Download into your TotalRecalls library layout.</li>
    </ol>
    <h2>Tips</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Keep the original Takeout zip as cold backup</li>
      <li>Use TotalRecalls output as your day-to-day readable layer</li>
      <li>Re-run when you generate a fresh Takeout</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Multi-provider reality</h2>
    <p>Many people use Gemini for some tasks and ChatGPT/Claude for others. A Takeout-only workflow is fine for Google — TotalRecalls exists so the rest of your assistants can live in the same archive philosophy.</p>

